 Arms the CCI CSR and both camera sensors at boot (erhai-cam-arm.service +
 erhai-cam-arm.sh) and ships the manual VCM focus / exposure helpers for the
 SC1320CS rear camera (i2c-10 slaves 0x0c / 0x36).  Also ships
 erhai-autofocus, a GTK4/GStreamer contrast-autofocus prototype that drives
 the kernel cn3927 lens subdev (V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE) with a Tenengrad
 sharpness scan; run it with the Snapshot preview closed.
 The erhai-cam-focus@erhai.local GNOME Shell extension is RETIRED (1.3 removes
 it): ErhaiCam (oneplus-erhai-erhaicam >= 1.5) owns focus AND exposure
 natively — an AE button (auto exposure on the NPU) and an AF button (auto
 focus on the NPU), each with a vertical manual slider when turned off.  The
 i2c helper scripts stay as manual CLI tools.
 VCM writes are granted to the desktop user via the included udev uaccess
 rules (CCI adapter + lens subdev); requires the kernel cn3927 module.
 1.4: the shipped erhai-autofocus is no longer a -g binary.  The DWARF of 1.3
 (and earlier) carried this pad's absolute build paths (the workspace tree and
 its tmp/gst-dev include dirs) into a public .deb; the builder now maps the
 prefix and strips the debug info, and refuses to pack a binary that still
 contains the build directory.  No functional change.

